    <title subtitle="" lang="en">Hello!</title>
    <description lang="en">This virtual learning object "Hello!" that makes part of the lesson No: 1, What's Your Name?, which in turn belongs to the Pre-Starter (Pre-A1) of the teaching of English as a Foreign Language, is intended to work on: say hello and goodbye in more or less formal situations, at different times of the day; introduce yourself to a class group or to a visitor at work. The grammar of this LO refers to: present tense of verb to be (am, is, are) in affirmative form: I, he, she, it. Also, the vocabulary considers: greetings; personal information: names, last names, titles; times of the day, days, seasons, e.g. Friday, Winter, Summer.</description>
    <keyword lang="en">
      <li>Greetings</li>
      <li>Personal Information</li>
      <li>Names</li>
      <li>Weekdays</li>
      <li>Seasons</li>
      <li>Simple present</li>
      <li>Affirmative forms</li>
      <li>Verb to be</li>
    </keyword>
